    "compliance.checks.iso_access_control.title": "Access control centrally defined",
    "compliance.checks.iso_access_control.desc": "Every API route must map to a declared access rule. Bee Flow keeps a machine-readable route registry plus role definitions, and a drift test verifies the declarations against the real route gates.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_access_control.fix": "Restore the access registry, its drift test and the role definitions shipped with the server, then review who holds admin roles under Security → Users.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_secure_auth.title": "Secure sign-in protections",
    "compliance.checks.iso_secure_auth.desc": "Sign-in must resist guessing and stale sessions: repeated failed unlocks trigger escalating lockouts, every request re-checks that the account still exists, and SSO keeps identities centrally managed.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_secure_auth.fix": "Enable a single sign-on provider (Google, Microsoft or Nextcloud) under Security → SSO, and keep the built-in lockout, session and password-policy modules unmodified.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_cryptography.title": "Strong encryption in use",
    "compliance.checks.iso_cryptography.desc": "User data is protected with envelope encryption: AES-256-GCM for content and Argon2id for key derivation, so the server never holds a usable copy of a user's keys.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_cryptography.fix": "Set MASTER_ENCRYPTION_KEY and SESSION_SECRET in the server environment and restart. Never modify the encryption module — the shipped AES-256-GCM / Argon2id configuration is the reviewed baseline.",

    "compliance.checks.iso_logging.title": "Security event logging live",
    "compliance.checks.iso_logging.desc": "A.8.15/8.16: the integration-activity and guardrail ledgers must keep receiving events — security-relevant actions can only be monitored if they are actually recorded.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_logging.fix": "Open Monitoring → Activity and confirm new events keep appearing. If the ledgers stay empty while people are working, check that the Privacy Shield and integration logging are switched on.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_deletion.title": "Data deletion enforced",
    "compliance.checks.iso_deletion.desc": "A.8.10: data past its retention window must actually disappear — the retention job runs daily and erasure requests are completed within their deadline.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_deletion.fix": "Open Compliance → Settings and check the retention job heartbeat; if the enforcer is not running, restart the server. Clear any overdue deletion requests in the DSR Inbox.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_dlp.title": "Data masking & leak prevention",
    "compliance.checks.iso_dlp.desc": "A.8.11/8.12: PII masking and outbound guardrails keep sensitive data from reaching external models — and the guardrail log should show them firing on real traffic.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_dlp.fix": "Open Security → Guardrails and enable both regex collections and PII detection. Once traffic flows, confirm guardrail events (redactions/blocks) appear in the log.",

    "compliance.checks.iso_incident_mgmt.title": "Security incident management",
    "compliance.checks.iso_incident_mgmt.desc": "A live incident register demonstrates that the incident process works: events are recorded, assessed and resolved before their notification deadline, with recipients ready to be alerted.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_incident_mgmt.fix": "Record and progress incidents under Compliance → Incidents, and add at least one notification recipient in Compliance → Settings.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_asset_inventory.title": "Information asset inventory",
    "compliance.checks.iso_asset_inventory.desc": "The workspace enumerates its own information assets from live configuration: AI providers, published agents and their models, knowledge bases, integration connections and MCP servers. The evidence of this check is the inventory itself.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_asset_inventory.fix": "Review the asset counts in the evidence. If agents run without a registered provider or assets are missing, register them in the AI settings and document the processing under Compliance → ROPA.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_suppliers.title": "Supplier and cloud service agreements",
    "compliance.checks.iso_suppliers.desc": "Every external operator the workspace actually sent data to in the last 30 days should be covered by a confirmed agreement (DPA/SCC) — cloud and EU-based suppliers included.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_suppliers.fix": "Confirm the agreement for each uncovered operator under Compliance → ROPA, or stop routing traffic to suppliers without a contract.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_evidence_integrity.title": "Compliance evidence chain intact",
    "compliance.checks.iso_evidence_integrity.desc": "Every check run appends an evidence row with a SHA-256 fingerprint. This check verifies the chain keeps growing and the stored fingerprints are valid, keeping audit evidence tamper-evident.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_evidence_integrity.fix": "Evidence is written automatically on every check run. If the chain is stale or fingerprints are missing, make sure the server and its compliance scheduler are running and the database is healthy.",
