    "compliance.checks.iso_vuln_mgmt.title": "Dependency vulnerabilities (GitHub)",
    "compliance.checks.iso_vuln_mgmt.desc": "Open Dependabot alerts on your monitored repositories must be triaged — a critical or high finding left open for more than a month means known-vulnerable code keeps shipping.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_vuln_mgmt.fix": "Enable Dependabot alerts on every monitored repository, give the connector token permission to read them, and fix or dismiss critical/high findings within 30 days.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_source_protection.title": "Source code branch protection",
    "compliance.checks.iso_source_protection.desc": "The default branch of every monitored repository must be protected: required reviews and no force pushes keep unreviewed changes and rewritten history out of the code that ships.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_source_protection.fix": "Turn on branch protection for the default branch of each repository, require at least one approving review, and keep force pushes disallowed.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_secure_coding.title": "Secret scanning in repositories",
    "compliance.checks.iso_secure_coding.desc": "GitHub secret scanning and push protection should be active on every monitored repository so leaked credentials are blocked at push time or caught right after they land.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_secure_coding.fix": "Enable secret scanning and push protection in the code security settings of each repository (or organisation-wide), and give the connector token permission to read the status.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_change_mgmt.title": "Change management on merges",
    "compliance.checks.iso_change_mgmt.desc": "A sample of recent merges into the default branch shows whether changes really go through review: merges without an independent approval, or merged by their own author, bypass the four-eyes principle.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_change_mgmt.fix": "Require pull-request reviews before merging and have someone other than the author perform the merge — the sample refreshes on the next evidence sweep.",
    "compliance.connector.github.title": "GitHub repository security",
    "compliance.connector.github.desc": "Reads vulnerability alerts, branch protection, secret scanning and merge-review posture from your repositories — evidence for A.8.4, A.8.8, A.8.28 and A.8.32.",

    "compliance.checks.iso_backups.title": "Server backups are fresh",
    "compliance.checks.iso_backups.desc": "Every cloud server should have a recent disk snapshot. The Scaleway connector reads the snapshot list per server and asserts that no server's newest backup falls behind more than a few days, so a failed disk never means lost data.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_backups.fix": "Enable a snapshot schedule for every Instance volume in the Scaleway console (or via the API), aim for at least one snapshot every 3 days per server, then re-run the sweep under ISO 27001 → Connectors.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_network_exposure.title": "Admin ports closed to the internet",
    "compliance.checks.iso_network_exposure.desc": "Firewall rules that open SSH or database ports (22, 5432, 6379, 3306) to 0.0.0.0/0 invite brute-force attacks and data theft. The connector reads every Scaleway security group and flags world-open admin ports; web ports 80/443 are normal and never flagged.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_network_exposure.fix": "Edit the flagged security groups in the Scaleway console: restrict admin ports to your VPN or office addresses, set the default inbound policy to drop, then re-run the sweep under ISO 27001 → Connectors.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_monitoring.title": "Log monitoring with alerting",
    "compliance.checks.iso_monitoring.desc": "Security events only help when someone sees them. The connector verifies that the OpenObserve log platform actually receives data and that at least one enabled alert rule notifies people, with enough retention left to investigate incidents afterwards.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_monitoring.fix": "Point your services at the OpenObserve ingest endpoint so streams receive data, create and enable at least one alert rule with a destination, and raise stream retention to 90 days or more.",
    "compliance.connector.scaleway.title": "Scaleway infrastructure",
    "compliance.connector.scaleway.desc": "Reads servers, Kubernetes clusters, snapshots and security groups from your Scaleway project with a read-only API key — evidence for backup freshness and network exposure.",
    "compliance.connector.openobserve.title": "OpenObserve monitoring",
    "compliance.connector.openobserve.desc": "Reads stream and alert configuration from your OpenObserve instance — evidence that logs are collected, retained and wired to alert someone.",

    "compliance.checks.iso_identity_hygiene.title": "Directory accounts kept clean",
    "compliance.checks.iso_identity_hygiene.desc": "Dormant accounts and weak MFA enrolment in the connected directory (Google Workspace or Microsoft Entra) are the easiest way into an organisation. This check reads the latest directory snapshot and flags dormant accounts above 1% of the active population and MFA enrolment below 90%.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_identity_hygiene.fix": "Disable or remove accounts that have not signed in for 90 days and enforce MFA enrolment for the rest. When a value shows as unknown, grant the reporting permission listed in the connector description so the sweep can measure it.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_workplace_software.title": "Workplace server software recorded",
    "compliance.checks.iso_workplace_software.desc": "The Nextcloud connector records the running server version and pending app updates in the evidence chain, so an auditor can see which workplace software was in use and exactly when it changed.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_workplace_software.fix": "Check the Nextcloud base URL and the admin app password on the connector, make sure the serverinfo app is enabled, then run a sweep so a version snapshot lands in the evidence chain.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_offboarding_feed.title": "HR feed for joiners and leavers",
    "compliance.checks.iso_offboarding_feed.desc": "Access reviews and offboarding are only as reliable as the employee list behind them. This check confirms the AFAS GetConnector designated as the HR feed answers and returns employee rows.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_offboarding_feed.fix": "Verify the AFAS environment URL, the AppConnector token and the GetConnector name in the connector settings, and make sure that GetConnector actually returns employee rows.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_ticketed_changes.title": "Changes tracked in tickets",
    "compliance.checks.iso_ticketed_changes.desc": "Recent activity in the designated YouTrack project shows operational changes run through tickets instead of ad-hoc work — the trail change management asks for.",
    "compliance.checks.iso_ticketed_changes.fix": "Point the connector at the project where operational changes are ticketed, or start recording changes there — 30 days without a single updated issue leaves no change trail.",
    "compliance.connector.google_workspace.title": "Google Workspace directory",
    "compliance.connector.google_workspace.desc": "Counts accounts, 2-Step enrolment, admins and dormant users via the Admin SDK — identity evidence for A.5.16–A.5.18.",
    "compliance.connector.microsoft_entra.title": "Microsoft Entra ID directory",
    "compliance.connector.microsoft_entra.desc": "Counts accounts, sign-in activity and admin roles via Microsoft Graph — identity evidence for A.5.16–A.5.18.",
    "compliance.connector.nextcloud.title": "Nextcloud server info",
    "compliance.connector.nextcloud.desc": "Reads the server version and pending app updates from the serverinfo API — software-hygiene evidence for A.8.19.",
    "compliance.connector.afas.title": "AFAS Profit HR feed",
    "compliance.connector.afas.desc": "Confirms the designated employee GetConnector returns rows — the HR population behind joiner/leaver reviews (A.6.5).",
    "compliance.connector.youtrack.title": "YouTrack change tickets",
    "compliance.connector.youtrack.desc": "Counts issues updated in the designated project over the last 30 days — proof that changes run through tickets (A.8.32).",

