    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_ear.desc": "GDPR Art. 32 requires appropriate technical measures. Bee-Flow uses AES-256-GCM envelope encryption with a master key derived from MASTER_ENCRYPTION_KEY.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_ear.fix": "Set the MASTER_ENCRYPTION_KEY and SESSION_SECRET environment variables on your server, then restart.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_eit.title": "Encryption in transit (TLS)",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_eit.desc": "All data between users and Bee-Flow must travel over TLS (HTTPS).",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_eit.fix": "Place Bee-Flow behind a TLS-terminating reverse proxy and set TRUST_PROXY=1 so auditors can confirm TLS.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_dlp.title": "Data Loss Prevention active",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_dlp.desc": "PII detection, regex guardrails and content moderation reduce the risk that sensitive data leaks to external models.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_dlp.fix": "Open Security → Guardrails and turn on regex collections, PII detection and moderation.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_log.title": "Access / guardrail logging",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_log.desc": "GDPR Art. 32 expects ongoing monitoring. The guardrail_events log shows what was blocked, redacted or allowed.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_log.fix": "Ensure guardrails are enabled so events are produced. If logging is silent, DLP may be disabled.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art33.title": "Breach notification readiness",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art33.desc": "Art. 33 requires notifying the supervisory authority within 72 hours of a personal-data breach. We detect bulk decrypts as an early signal.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art33.fix": "Add at least one email under \"Breach notification recipients\" in Compliance → Settings.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art37.title": "DPO appointed",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art37.desc": "A Data Protection Officer is mandatory when you process personal data at scale (Art. 37).",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art37.fix": "Fill in DPO name and email in Compliance → Settings.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art12.title": "Privacy notice published",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art12.desc": "Data subjects must find, in plain language, how their data is processed (Art. 12-14).",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art12.fix": "Publish your privacy notice and paste its URL in Compliance → Settings.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art44.title": "International transfers controlled",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art44.desc": "Using an external LLM exports personal data outside the EU. Art. 44-46 requires SCCs/DPA or equivalent safeguards.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art44.fix": "Either switch the agent(s) to self-hosted models, or register each external provider with a signed DPA/SCC in your records.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art50.title": "AI disclosure to users",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art50.desc": "The EU AI Act Art. 50 requires that end users are informed that they are interacting with an AI system.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art50.fix": "Add a line like \"You are chatting with an AI assistant\" to the system prompt or welcome banner of each published agent.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art13.title": "Transparency: agent described",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art13.desc": "Art. 13 expects users to understand the purpose, limitations and provider of the AI system.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art13.fix": "Fill in a meaningful description (30+ characters) for each agent in Admin → Agents.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art5_1_e.title": "Storage limitation enforced",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art5_1_e.desc": "Art. 5(1)(e) — personal data may only be kept as long as needed. A retention window plus an active cleanup job proves data is not kept forever.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art5_1_e.fix": "Set a default retention window in Compliance → Settings; the retention job then enforces it automatically.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art15.title": "Access requests answered on time",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art15.desc": "Art. 15 gives every person the right to a copy of their data. Requests must be answered within 30 days.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art15.fix": "Open Compliance → DSR Inbox and fulfil the open access requests before their 30-day deadline.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art17.title": "Deletion requests fulfilled",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art17.desc": "Art. 17 (right to erasure) — deletion requests must be honoured without undue delay, at most within 30 days.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art17.fix": "Open Compliance → DSR Inbox and fulfil the open deletion requests before their 30-day deadline.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art30.title": "Processing register (ROPA) reviewed",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art30.desc": "Art. 30 requires an up-to-date record of processing activities. Bee-Flow generates it from your live configuration; a periodic review keeps it accurate.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art30.fix": "Open Compliance → ROPA, check that the activities and processors are correct, and mark the register as reviewed.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art35.title": "DPIA for high-risk agents",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art35.desc": "Art. 35 requires a Data Protection Impact Assessment before high-risk processing — e.g. agents handling personal data through external models.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art35.fix": "Open Compliance → DPIA and complete (or attest) an assessment for each flagged agent.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art28.title": "Processor agreements (DPAs)",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art28.desc": "Art. 28 requires a binding data-processing agreement with every processor that handles personal data on your behalf — EU-based ones included.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art28.fix": "Open Compliance → ROPA and attest the signed DPA/SCC for each observed processor.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_eff.title": "DLP effectiveness",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_eff.desc": "Art. 32(1)(d) requires regularly testing that security measures actually work. DLP that is switched on but never produces a single guardrail event under real traffic is usually not in the request path.",
    "compliance.checks.gdpr_art32_eff.fix": "Open Security → Guardrails and verify the shield's scope and services; send a test message containing dummy PII and confirm an event is logged.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art4.title": "AI literacy programme",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art4.desc": "EU AI Act Art. 4 (in force since Feb 2025): staff operating AI systems must have a sufficient level of AI literacy — training, guidelines or equivalent measures.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art4.fix": "Confirm your AI-literacy measures (and optionally link the training material) under Compliance → Settings. Re-confirm annually.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art26.title": "Human oversight for high-risk agents",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art26.desc": "Art. 26 deployer obligations: high-risk AI use needs assigned human oversight with the competence and authority to intervene.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art26.fix": "Open Compliance → DPIA and fill in the \"Human oversight\" answer for each flagged agent — name the role who reviews its output.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art26_6.title": "AI activity logs kept 6+ months",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art26_6.desc": "Art. 12 / 26(6): automatically generated logs of high-risk AI systems must be retained for at least six months.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art26_6.fix": "Do not purge the integration-activity and guardrail logs below six months; if a cleanup job trims them, raise its window.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art53.title": "GPAI model inventory",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art53.desc": "Art. 53 GPAI transparency (in force since Aug 2025): know which general-purpose models your workspace routes data to, and that each external provider is covered by a safeguard.",
    "compliance.checks.aia_art53.fix": "Review the model inventory in this check's evidence and attest the SCC/DPA for each external provider under Compliance → ROPA.",

